From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:41:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] libeffects: don't register ViPER twice

loadViperEffect() runs after the effects XML has loaded and registers
libv4a_re.so as library "v4a_re" without checking whether its effect
uuid (90380da3-8536-4744-a6a3-5731970e640f) is already known. When a
ViPER4Android module also adds the library and effect to
audio_effects.xml, the factory ends up with two libraries for one
effect and lists the effect twice. Return early when findEffect()
already has the uuid.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019koBAc5T4WjFHL6bYvou5m
---
 media/libeffects/factory/EffectsFactory.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/media/libeffects/factory/EffectsFactory.c b/media/libeffects/factory/EffectsFactory.c
index 3bd8b87d26..2ae304e000 100644
--- a/media/libeffects/factory/EffectsFactory.c
+++ b/media/libeffects/factory/EffectsFactory.c
@@ -643,6 +643,14 @@ void loadViperEffect() {
     void *libHandle = NULL;
     audio_effect_library_t *libDesc = NULL;
     const char *libPath = NULL;
+    lib_entry_t *registeredLib = NULL;
+
+    // An audio_effects.xml entry (e.g. from a ViPER module) may have registered it already
+    if (findEffect(NULL, &kViperImplUuid, &registeredLib, NULL) == 0) {
+        ALOGI("loadViperEffect: ViPER effect already registered by library %s, skipping",
+              registeredLib->name);
+        return;
+    }
 
     for (int i = 0; kViperLibPaths[i] != NULL; i++) {
         if (access(kViperLibPaths[i], R_OK) == 0) {
-- 
